I was running my standard Barbarian, in the Heart of Ahriman quest (I also
found the silver bell on him, the *1st* time I have ever seen THAT happen..)
(and yes, I have never finished, it is true =)...anyways. I took a few
potshots at Thoth Amon with a juiced up Mojo (nothing else really special on
me, didn't even get 1 wishing item so far...)..and invoked the Heart. Found
myself floating around. Suddenly, Thoth goes berserk and starts draining
my stats, and disintegrating my armor bit by bit, yelling:

"So, steal the Heart of Ahriman, will you? I will have it soon, yes. As well
as your life." (or something only slightly different)

Well, I was more amused and interested than anything else. Suddenly, when 
invading the 'real' room he is usually in, he gates in a handful of
monsters, and repeats his threat of death. Suddenly, I hear this "buuuurp!"
and Mr. Purple Worm (screw the purple dinosaurs...;)...purple worms rock!)
appears and eats him immediately after he says this. He dies, with a scream.
=) =) =)

I was in danger of dying afterward from the Titan he gated in, as well
as the mumak (I *loathe* those puppies...=)...cause I always meet them
when overburdened =) (very overburdened))...except he gated in Mr.
Cockatrice too, who conveniently statued everything for me. =) How kind!
(I even let him live for it ;).

I did lose 2 levels (went from 19, which I'd gotten to in a graveyard,
my 1st =(, by eating wraiths)...from 19 to 17. I do have a ?, I suppose..
I've finally been able to try many fun things this game without being
trampled upon when overburdened, like writing blessed genocide scrolls.
I had genocided all lich class, all troll class (handy for whipping
through the barb quest =) ) and all vampire class monsters. I hit a poly
trap and it asked me what monster I wanted to become (since I've learned
to travel with my damn poly control ring on =) and I said, with some
hesitation, vampire lord. I thought there was a small chance of me dying,
since I had fried all vamp types before (all blessed geno scrolls, you see),
but instead it changed me into a "new man". The stats were comparable...
the *level* went from 19 to 17. Why the *hell* did this happen? =)

Please e-mail as I don't usually read this group (the answer, if any)...
but I hope you enjoy the story. I *gotta* try that on the Wizard.

=)

